<h3 data-start=3D"3295" data-end=3D"3334">2.4. Attention au garbage collect=
or</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3336" data-end=3D"3689">
<li data-start=3D"3336" data-end=3D"3493">
<p data-start=3D"3338" data-end=3D"3493">PHP ex=C3=A9cute un garbage collec=
tor (GC) qui supprime les donn=C3=A9es de session expir=C3=A9es al=C3=A9ato=
irement, selon <code data-start=3D"3442" data-end=3D"3466">session.gc_proba=
bility</code> et <code data-start=3D"3470" data-end=3D"3490">session.gc_div=
isor</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3494" data-end=3D"3572">
<p data-start=3D"3496" data-end=3D"3572">Par d=C3=A9faut, la probabilit=C3=
=A9 que le GC s=E2=80=99ex=C3=A9cute =C3=A0 chaque requ=C3=AAte est de 1%.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3573" data-end=3D"3689">
<p data-start=3D"3575" data-end=3D"3689">Si vous avez plusieurs serveurs (c=
luster), le GC ne s=E2=80=99ex=C3=A9cute que sur un seul serveur, ce qui pe=
ut poser probl=C3=A8me.</p>
</li>
</ul>
