<p data-start=3D"4232" data-end=3D"4248"><strong data-start=3D"4232" data-e=
nd=3D"4246">Pourquoi ?</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"4249" data-end=3D"4485">
<li data-start=3D"4249" data-end=3D"4310">
<p data-start=3D"4251" data-end=3D"4310"><code data-start=3D"4251" data-end=
=3D"4259">secure</code> emp=C3=AAche l=E2=80=99envoi du cookie sur HTTP non=
 s=C3=A9curis=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4311" data-end=3D"4392">
<p data-start=3D"4313" data-end=3D"4392"><code data-start=3D"4313" data-end=
=3D"4323">httponly</code> emp=C3=AAche le vol du cookie par du code JavaScr=
ipt malveillant (XSS).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4393" data-end=3D"4485">
<p data-start=3D"4395" data-end=3D"4485"><code data-start=3D"4395" data-end=
=3D"4405">samesite</code> emp=C3=AAche l=E2=80=99envoi du cookie lors de re=
qu=C3=AAtes cross-site, limitant le risque CSRF.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4487" data-end=3D"4490">
