<hr data-start=3D"5916" data-end=3D"5919">
<h2 data-start=3D"5921" data-end=3D"5966">7. Visibilit=C3=A9 et interfaces =
/ abstractions</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"5968" data-end=3D"6196">
<li data-start=3D"5968" data-end=3D"6036">
<p data-start=3D"5970" data-end=3D"6036">Les m=C3=A9thodes d=C3=A9finies da=
ns une interface sont toujours <code data-start=3D"6025" data-end=3D"6033">=
public</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6037" data-end=3D"6111">
<p data-start=3D"6039" data-end=3D"6111">Une classe impl=C3=A9mentant une i=
nterface doit respecter cette visibilit=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6112" data-end=3D"6196">
<p data-start=3D"6114" data-end=3D"6196">Vous ne pouvez pas d=C3=A9finir un=
e m=C3=A9thode d=E2=80=99interface comme <code data-start=3D"6171" data-end=
=3D"6180">private</code> ou <code data-start=3D"6184" data-end=3D"6195">pro=
tected</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6198" data-end=3D"6201">
<h2 data-start=3D"6203" data-end=3D"6250">8. Meilleures pratiques pour l=E2=
=80=99encapsulation</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"6252" data-end=3D"6294">8.1. Pr=C3=A9f=C3=A9rez les propr=
i=C3=A9t=C3=A9s <code data-start=3D"6285" data-end=3D"6294">private</code><=
/h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6296" data-end=3D"6445">
<li data-start=3D"6296" data-end=3D"6390">
<p data-start=3D"6298" data-end=3D"6390">Prot=C3=A9gez vos donn=C3=A9es ave=
c <code data-start=3D"6324" data-end=3D"6333">private</code> pour limiter a=
u maximum les effets de bord inattendus.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6391" data-end=3D"6445">
<p data-start=3D"6393" data-end=3D"6445">Utilisez des getters/setters pour =
contr=C3=B4ler l=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6447" data-end=3D"6512">8.2. Utilisez <code data-start=3D=
"6465" data-end=3D"6476">protected</code> uniquement pour l=E2=80=99h=C3=A9=
ritage contr=C3=B4l=C3=A9</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6514" data-end=3D"6645">
<li data-start=3D"6514" data-end=3D"6645">
<p data-start=3D"6516" data-end=3D"6645"><code data-start=3D"6516" data-end=
=3D"6527">protected</code> est utile quand vous voulez que les classes enfa=
nts puissent acc=C3=A9der aux donn=C3=A9es internes, mais pas le reste du c=
ode.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6647" data-end=3D"6697">8.3. Gardez les propri=C3=A9t=C3=
=A9s <code data-start=3D"6678" data-end=3D"6686">public</code> au minimum</=
h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6699" data-end=3D"6879">
<li data-start=3D"6699" data-end=3D"6795">
<p data-start=3D"6701" data-end=3D"6795">Les propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9s publiques=
 exposent la structure interne et peuvent rendre votre code fragile.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6796" data-end=3D"6879">
<p data-start=3D"6798" data-end=3D"6879">R=C3=A9servez <code data-start=3D"=
6807" data-end=3D"6815">public</code> principalement pour des constantes ou=
 des m=C3=A9thodes d=E2=80=99interface.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6881" data-end=3D"6884">
