 de donn=C3=A9es : <code data-start=3D"299" data-end=3D"306">fetch</code>, =
<code data-start=3D"308" data-end=3D"318">fetchAll</code></h3>
<hr data-start=3D"320" data-end=3D"323">
<h2 data-start=3D"325" data-end=3D"346">=F0=9F=94=B0 1. Introduction</h2>
<p data-start=3D"348" data-end=3D"559">Quand vous effectuez une requ=C3=AAt=
e <code data-start=3D"381" data-end=3D"389">SELECT</code> avec PDO, le r=C3=
=A9sultat est encapsul=C3=A9 dans un <strong data-start=3D"434" data-end=3D=
"466">objet de type <code data-start=3D"450" data-end=3D"464">PDOStatement<=
/code></strong>. Pour en extraire les donn=C3=A9es, PDO vous offre plusieur=
s m=C3=A9thodes, les plus courantes =C3=A9tant :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"561" data-end=3D"663">
<li data-start=3D"561" data-end=3D"604">
<p data-start=3D"563" data-end=3D"604"><code data-start=3D"563" data-end=3D=
"572">fetch()</code> : r=C3=A9cup=C3=A8re <strong data-start=3D"584" data-e=
nd=3D"603">une seule ligne</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"605" data-end=3D"663">
<p data-start=3D"607" data-end=3D"663"><code data-start=3D"607" data-end=3D=
"619">fetchAll()</code> : r=C3=A9cup=C3=A8re <strong data-start=3D"631" dat=
a-end=3D"662">toutes les lignes d=E2=80=99un coup</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"665" data-end=3D"797">Ces m=C3=A9thodes peuvent aussi pren=
dre des options comme <code data-start=3D"718" data-end=3D"736">PDO::FETCH_=
ASSOC</code>, <code data-start=3D"738" data-end=3D"754">PDO::FETCH_OBJ</cod=
e>, etc., pour contr=C3=B4ler le format de retour.</p>
