<ul data-start=3D"5630" data-end=3D"6061">
<li data-start=3D"5630" data-end=3D"5733">
<p data-start=3D"5632" data-end=3D"5733"><strong data-start=3D"5632" data-e=
nd=3D"5675">Utiliser <code data-start=3D"5643" data-end=3D"5653">static::</=
code> au lieu de <code data-start=3D"5665" data-end=3D"5673">self::</code><=
/strong> dans les m=C3=A9thodes statiques qui doivent =C3=AAtre extensibles=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5734" data-end=3D"5838">
<p data-start=3D"5736" data-end=3D"5838">Pr=C3=A9f=C3=A9rer <code data-star=
t=3D"5745" data-end=3D"5755">static::</code> dans les m=C3=A9thodes factory=
, m=C3=A9thode retournant une instance de la classe appelante.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5839" data-end=3D"5913">
<p data-start=3D"5841" data-end=3D"5913">Comprendre bien la diff=C3=A9rence=
 entre <code data-start=3D"5877" data-end=3D"5885">self::</code>, <code dat=
a-start=3D"5887" data-end=3D"5897">static::</code>, et <code data-start=3D"=
5902" data-end=3D"5912">parent::</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5914" data-end=3D"5997">
<p data-start=3D"5916" data-end=3D"5997">Ne pas abuser de LSB : c=E2=80=99e=
st un outil puissant, mais parfois source de confusion.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5998" data-end=3D"6061">
<p data-start=3D"6000" data-end=3D"6061">Toujours tester le comportement da=
ns une hi=C3=A9rarchie complexe.</p>
</li>
</ul>
