-start=3D"0" data-end=3D"271">Bien s=C3=BBr ! Voici un tutoriel complet et =
approfondi sur les <strong data-start=3D"59" data-end=3D"110">Patterns de c=
onception (Design Patterns) en PHP</strong>, de niveau d=C3=A9butant =C3=A0=
 expert. Ce tutoriel couvre les principes, plusieurs patterns classiques et=
 leurs mises en =C5=93uvre, ainsi que les bonnes pratiques associ=C3=A9es.<=
/p>
<hr data-start=3D"273" data-end=3D"276">
<h1 data-start=3D"278" data-end=3D"342">Tutoriel PHP Avanc=C3=A9 =E2=80=94 =
Patterns de conception (Design Patterns)</h1>
<hr data-start=3D"344" data-end=3D"347">
<h2 data-start=3D"349" data-end=3D"364">Introduction</h2>
<p data-start=3D"366" data-end=3D"598">Les <strong data-start=3D"370" data-=
end=3D"396">patterns de conception</strong> sont des solutions =C3=A9prouv=
=C3=A9es =C3=A0 des probl=C3=A8mes r=C3=A9currents de conception logicielle=
. Ils permettent d=E2=80=99=C3=A9crire un code plus clair, maintenable, r=
=C3=A9utilisable, et facilitent la collaboration dans les projets.</p>
<p data-start=3D"600" data-end=3D"853">Les design patterns ne sont pas sp=
=C3=A9cifiques =C3=A0 un langage, mais leur impl=C3=A9mentation varie selon=
 la syntaxe et les particularit=C3=A9s du langage utilis=C3=A9. En PHP, ils=
 sont tr=C3=A8s utiles pour structurer les applications, notamment en progr=
ammation orient=C3=A9e objet.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"855" data-end=3D"858">
<h2 data-start=3D"860" data-end=3D"895">Pourquoi utiliser les patterns ?</h=
2>
<ul data-start=3D"897" data-end=3D"1220">
<li data-start=3D"897" data-end=3D"984">
<p data-start=3D"899" data-end=3D"984"><strong data-start=3D"899" data-end=
=3D"918">R=C3=A9utilisabilit=C3=A9</strong> : Eviter de r=C3=A9inventer la =
roue, utiliser des solutions =C3=A9prouv=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"985" data-end=3D"1068">
<p data-start=3D"987" data-end=3D"1068"><strong data-start=3D"987" data-end=
=3D"997">Clart=C3=A9</strong> : Faciliter la compr=C3=A9hension du code gr=
=C3=A2ce =C3=A0 des concepts bien connus.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1069" data-end=3D"1137">
<p data-start=3D"1071" data-end=3D"1137"><strong data-start=3D"1071" data-e=
nd=3D"1086">Maintenance</strong> : Simplifier l=E2=80=99=C3=A9volution et l=
a correction du code.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1138" data-end=3D"1220">
<p data-start=3D"1140" data-end=3D"1220"><strong data-start=3D"1140" data-e=
nd=3D"1157">Communication</strong> : Les patterns sont un vocabulaire parta=
g=C3=A9 entre d=C3=A9veloppeurs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1222" data-end=3D"1225">
<h2 data-start=3D"1227" data-end=3D"1271">Classification rapide des design =
patterns</h2>
<ol data-start=3D"1273" data-end=3D"1658">
<li data-start=3D"1273" data-end=3D"1399">
<p data-start=3D"1276" data-end=3D"1399"><strong data-start=3D"1276" data-e=
nd=3D"1300">Patterns de cr=C3=A9ation</strong> : Concernent la cr=C3=A9atio=
n d=E2=80=99objets. Ex. : Singleton, Factory, Abstract Factory, Builder, Pr=
ototype.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1400" data-end=3D"1530">
<p data-start=3D"1403" data-end=3D"1530"><strong data-start=3D"1403" data-e=
nd=3D"1427">Patterns structurels</strong> : Concernent la composition des c=
lasses ou objets. Ex. : Adapter, Decorator, Facade, Composite, Proxy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1531" data-end=3D"1658">
<p data-start=3D"1534" data-end=3D"1658"><strong data-start=3D"1534" data-e=
nd=3D"1562">Patterns comportementaux</strong> : Concernent la communication=
 entre objets. Ex. : Observer, Strategy, Command, Iterator, State.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"1660" data-end=3D"1663">
<h1 data-start=3D"1665" data-end=3D"1687">1. Pattern Singleton</h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"1689" data-end=3D"1696">But</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1697" data-end=3D"1799">Garantir qu=E2=80=99une classe n=
=E2=80=99a qu=E2=80=99une seule instance, et fournir un point d=E2=80=99acc=
=C3=A8s global =C3=A0 cette instance.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1801" data-end=3D"1823">Quand l=E2=80=99utiliser ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1824" data-end=3D"1908">
<li data-start=3D"1824" data-end=3D"1858">
<p data-start=3D"1826" data-end=3D"1858">Connexion =C3=A0 une base de donn=
=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1859" data-end=3D"1891">
<p data-start=3D"1861" data-end=3D"1891">Gestionnaire de configuration.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1892" data-end=3D"1908">
<p data-start=3D"1894" data-end=3D"1908">Logger global.</p>
</li>
