<h1 data-start=3D"8467" data-end=3D"8537">6. Bonnes pratiques g=C3=A9n=C3=
=A9rales pour l=E2=80=99utilisation des patterns en PHP</h1>
<ul data-start=3D"8539" data-end=3D"9017">
<li data-start=3D"8539" data-end=3D"8626">
<p data-start=3D"8541" data-end=3D"8626"><strong data-start=3D"8541" data-e=
nd=3D"8563">Ne pas surutiliser</strong> : un pattern mal adapt=C3=A9 peut c=
omplexifier inutilement le code.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8627" data-end=3D"8711">
<p data-start=3D"8629" data-end=3D"8711"><strong data-start=3D"8629" data-e=
nd=3D"8654">S=E2=80=99adapter au contexte</strong> : choisir le pattern en =
fonction du probl=C3=A8me =C3=A0 r=C3=A9soudre.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8712" data-end=3D"8811">
<p data-start=3D"8714" data-end=3D"8811"><strong data-start=3D"8714" data-e=
nd=3D"8745">Respecter le principe SOLID</strong> : patterns doivent facilit=
er la maintenabilit=C3=A9 et la flexibilit=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8812" data-end=3D"8880">
<p data-start=3D"8814" data-end=3D"8880"><strong data-start=3D"8814" data-e=
nd=3D"8839">Documenter clairement</strong> l=E2=80=99utilisation des patter=
ns dans le code.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8881" data-end=3D"8940">
<p data-start=3D"8883" data-end=3D"8940"><strong data-start=3D"8883" data-e=
nd=3D"8910">Utiliser les interfaces</strong> pour garantir la flexibilit=C3=
=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8941" data-end=3D"9017">
<p data-start=3D"8943" data-end=3D"9017"><strong data-start=3D"8943" data-e=
nd=3D"8976">=C3=89viter les singletons abusifs</strong> qui peuvent rendre =
les tests difficiles.</p>
</li>
</ul>
