>Avec plaisir ! Voici un tutoriel complet et approfondi sur les <strong dat=
a-start=3D"63" data-end=3D"101">PSR (PHP Standard Recommendations)</strong>=
, couvrant les concepts depuis le niveau d=C3=A9butant jusqu=E2=80=99au niv=
eau expert, avec des explications claires et d=C3=A9taill=C3=A9es. Ce sujet=
 est fondamental pour =C3=A9crire du code PHP propre, standardis=C3=A9, mai=
ntenable et compatible avec l=E2=80=99=C3=A9cosyst=C3=A8me moderne.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"344" data-end=3D"347">
<h1 data-start=3D"349" data-end=3D"437">Tutoriel complet : PSR (PHP Standar=
d Recommendations) =E2=80=93 Normes et bonnes pratiques PHP</h1>
<hr data-start=3D"439" data-end=3D"442">
<h2 data-start=3D"444" data-end=3D"459">Introduction</h2>
<p data-start=3D"461" data-end=3D"739">Les <strong data-start=3D"465" data-=
end=3D"472">PSR</strong> sont des recommandations standardis=C3=A9es =C3=A9=
mises par le <strong data-start=3D"526" data-end=3D"537">PHP-FIG</strong> (=
PHP Framework Interoperability Group). Elles visent =C3=A0 uniformiser la m=
ani=C3=A8re dont les d=C3=A9veloppeurs =C3=A9crivent du code PHP, facilitan=
t ainsi l=E2=80=99interop=C3=A9rabilit=C3=A9 entre biblioth=C3=A8ques, fram=
eworks et projets.</p>
<p data-start=3D"741" data-end=3D"773">Ces recommandations concernent :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"775" data-end=3D"920">
<li data-start=3D"775" data-end=3D"793">
<p data-start=3D"777" data-end=3D"793">Le style de code</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"794" data-end=3D"837">
<p data-start=3D"796" data-end=3D"837">L=E2=80=99organisation des fichiers =
et namespaces</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"838" data-end=3D"853">
<p data-start=3D"840" data-end=3D"853">L=E2=80=99autoloading</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"854" data-end=3D"866">
<p data-start=3D"856" data-end=3D"866">Le logging</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"867" data-end=3D"900">
<p data-start=3D"869" data-end=3D"900">Les interfaces, les middlewares</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"901" data-end=3D"920">
<p data-start=3D"903" data-end=3D"920">Et plus encore...</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"922" data-end=3D"1059">Adopter les PSR est une excellente =
pratique pour garantir un code clair, lisible, et compatible avec la majori=
t=C3=A9 des outils PHP modernes.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1061" data-end=3D"1064">
<h2 data-start=3D"1066" data-end=3D"1109">Partie 1 : Comprendre PHP-FIG et =
les PSR</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"1111" data-end=3D"1114">
<h3 data-start=3D"1116" data-end=3D"1146">1. Qu=E2=80=99est-ce que PHP-FIG =
?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1148" data-end=3D"1419">
<li data-start=3D"1148" data-end=3D"1262">
<p data-start=3D"1150" data-end=3D"1262"><strong data-start=3D"1150" data-e=
nd=3D"1190">PHP Framework Interoperability Group</strong> : un groupe de d=
=C3=A9veloppeurs de frameworks et biblioth=C3=A8ques PHP majeurs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1263" data-end=3D"1353">
<p data-start=3D"1265" data-end=3D"1353">Objectif : cr=C3=A9er des standard=
s communs pour =C3=A9viter la fragmentation de l=E2=80=99=C3=A9cosyst=C3=A8=
me PHP.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1354" data-end=3D"1419">
<p data-start=3D"1356" data-end=3D"1419">Chaque recommandation est un PSR (=
PHP Standard Recommendation).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1421" data-end=3D"1424">
<h3 data-start=3D"1426" data-end=3D"1471">2. Diff=C3=A9rence entre PSR, RFC=
 et standards</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1473" data-end=3D"1628">
<li data-start=3D"1473" data-end=3D"1522">
<p data-start=3D"1475" data-end=3D"1522"><strong data-start=3D"1475" data-e=
nd=3D"1482">PSR</strong> : propositions officiellement adopt=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1523" data-end=3D"1579">
<p data-start=3D"1525" data-end=3D"1579"><strong data-start=3D"1525" data-e=
nd=3D"1532">RFC</strong> : propositions discut=C3=A9es, en cours d=E2=80=99=
adoption.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1580" data-end=3D"1628">
<p data-start=3D"1582" data-end=3D"1628">PSR sont publi=C3=A9es, maintenues=
 et mises =C3=A0 jour.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1630" data-end=3D"1633">
<h3 data-start=3D"1635" data-end=3D"1667">3. Pourquoi suivre les PSR ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1669" data-end=3D"1833">
<li data-start=3D"1669" data-end=3D"1697">
<p data-start=3D"1671" data-end=3D"1697">Facilite la collaboration.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1698" data-end=3D"1728">
<p data-start=3D"1700" data-end=3D"1728">Am=C3=A9liore la qualit=C3=A9 du c=
ode.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1729" data-end=3D"1766">
<p data-start=3D"1731" data-end=3D"1766">Rend les biblioth=C3=A8ques compat=
ibles.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1767" data-end=3D"1833">
<p data-start=3D"1769" data-end=3D"1833">Permet d=E2=80=99utiliser des outi=
ls tiers qui respectent ces standards.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1835" data-end=3D"1838">
<h2 data-start=3D"1840" data-end=3D"1881">Partie 2 : Les PSR les plus impor=
tants</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"1883" data-end=3D"1886">
<h3 data-start=3D"1888" data-end=3D"1943">1. PSR-1 : Basic Coding Standard =
(Standard de base)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1945" data-end=3D"2295">
<li data-start=3D"1945" data-end=3D"2001">
<p data-start=3D"1947" data-end=3D"2001">D=C3=A9finit les bases d=E2=80=99u=
n code PHP lisible et compatible.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2002" data-end=3D"2295">
<p data-start=3D"2004" data-end=3D"2017">Points cl=C3=A9s :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2020" data-end=3D"2295">
<li data-start=3D"2020" data-end=3D"2077">
<p data-start=3D"2022" data-end=3D"2077">Fichiers PHP doivent commencer par=
 <code data-start=3D"2057" data-end=3D"2064">&lt;?php</code> et non <code d=
ata-start=3D"2072" data-end=3D"2076">&lt;?</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2080" data-end=3D"2102">
<p data-start=3D"2082" data-end=3D"2102">Utilisation d=E2=80=99UTF-8.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2105" data-end=3D"2141">
<p data-start=3D"2107" data-end=3D"2141">Nommage des classes en PascalCase.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2144" data-end=3D"2180">
<p data-start=3D"2146" data-end=3D"2180">Nommage des m=C3=A9thodes en camel=
Case.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2183" data-end=3D"2250">
<p data-start=3D"2185" data-end=3D"2250">Pas de sortie directe (echo, print=
) dans les fichiers de classes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2253" data-end=3D"2295">
<p data-start=3D"2255" data-end=3D"2295">Pas de caract=C3=A8res BOM (Byte O=
rder Mark).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2297" data-end=3D"2300">
<h3 data-start=3D"2302" data-end=3D"2351">2. PSR-2 : Coding Style Guide (St=
yle de code)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2353" data-end=3D"2862">
<li data-start=3D"2353" data-end=3D"2373">
<p data-start=3D"2355" data-end=3D"2373">Compl=C3=A8te la PSR-1.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2374" data-end=3D"2862">
<p data-start=3D"2376" data-end=3D"2408">Recommandations d=C3=A9taill=C3=A9=
es sur :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2411" data-end=3D"2862">
<li data-start=3D"2411" data-end=3D"2457">
<p data-start=3D"2413" data-end=3D"2457">Indentation (4 espaces, pas de tab=
ulations).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2460" data-end=3D"2504">
<p data-start=3D"2462" data-end=3D"2504">Longueur max d=E2=80=99une ligne :=
 120 caract=C3=A8res.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2507" data-end=3D"2539">
<p data-start=3D"2509" data-end=3D"2539">Espaces autour des op=C3=A9rateurs=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2542" data-end=3D"2620">
<p data-start=3D"2544" data-end=3D"2620">Utilisation des accolades <code da=
ta-start=3D"2570" data-end=3D"2574">{}</code> sur la m=C3=AAme ligne pour l=
es fonctions/classes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2623" data-end=3D"2710">
<p data-start=3D"2625" data-end=3D"2710">Espacement avant les parenth=C3=A8=
ses dans les structures de contr=C3=B4le (<code data-start=3D"2691" data-en=
d=3D"2695">if</code>, <code data-start=3D"2697" data-end=3D"2702">for</code=
>, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2713" data-end=3D"2773">
<p data-start=3D"2715" data-end=3D"2773">Pas d=E2=80=99espace entre nom de =
fonction et parenth=C3=A8se ouvrante.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2776" data-end=3D"2862">
<p data-start=3D"2778" data-end=3D"2862">Les blocs <code data-start=3D"2788=
" data-end=3D"2794">else</code> et <code data-start=3D"2798" data-end=3D"28=
06">elseif</code> doivent =C3=AAtre sur la m=C3=AAme ligne que l=E2=80=99ac=
colade fermante.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2864" data-end=3D"2867">
<h3 data-start=3D"2869" data-end=3D"2904">3. PSR-4 : Autoloading standard</=
h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2906" data-end=3D"3254">
<li data-start=3D"2906" data-end=3D"2926">
<p data-start=3D"2908" data-end=3D"2926">Remplace la PSR-0.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2927" data-end=3D"2982">
<p data-start=3D"2929" data-end=3D"2982">Norme recommand=C3=A9e pour l=E2=
=80=99autoloading des classes PHP.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2983" data-end=3D"3213">
<p data-start=3D"2985" data-end=3D"2995">Principe :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2998" data-end=3D"3213">
<li data-start=3D"2998" data-end=3D"3057">
<p data-start=3D"3000" data-end=3D"3057">Les namespaces correspondent =C3=
=A0 la structure des dossiers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3060" data-end=3D"3127">
<p data-start=3D"3062" data-end=3D"3127">Une classe <code data-start=3D"307=
3" data-end=3D"3090">Acme\Log\Writer</code> se trouve dans <code data-start=
=3D"3106" data-end=3D"3126">src/Log/Writer.php</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3130" data-end=3D"3213">
<p data-start=3D"3132" data-end=3D"3213">Permet d=E2=80=99utiliser l=E2=80=
=99autoloading sans avoir =C3=A0 inclure manuellement chaque fichier.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3214" data-end=3D"3254">
<p data-start=3D"3216" data-end=3D"3254">Composer supporte nativement la PS=
R-4.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3256" data-end=3D"3259">
<h3 data-start=3D"3261" data-end=3D"3292">4. PSR-3 : Logger Interface</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3294" data-end=3D"3645">
<li data-start=3D"3294" data-end=3D"3360">
<p data-start=3D"3296" data-end=3D"3360">Standardise une interface de logge=
r (<code data-start=3D"3333" data-end=3D"3358">Psr\Log\LoggerInterface</cod=
e>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3361" data-end=3D"3422">
<p data-start=3D"3363" data-end=3D"3422">Permet d=E2=80=99utiliser des syst=
=C3=A8mes de logging interchangeables.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3423" data-end=3D"3544">
<p data-start=3D"3425" data-end=3D"3544">M=C3=A9thodes principales : <code =
data-start=3D"3448" data-end=3D"3461">emergency()</code>, <code data-start=
=3D"3463" data-end=3D"3472">alert()</code>, <code data-start=3D"3474" data-=
end=3D"3486">critical()</code>, <code data-start=3D"3488" data-end=3D"3497"=
>error()</code>, <code data-start=3D"3499" data-end=3D"3510">warning()</cod=
e>, <code data-start=3D"3512" data-end=3D"3522">notice()</code>, <code data=
-start=3D"3524" data-end=3D"3532">info()</code>, <code data-start=3D"3534" =
data-end=3D"3543">debug()</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3545" data-end=3D"3645">
<p data-start=3D"3547" data-end=3D"3645">Les biblioth=C3=A8ques peuvent uti=
liser cette interface pour accepter n=E2=80=99importe quel logger compatibl=
e.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3647" data-end=3D"3650">
<h3 data-start=3D"3652" data-end=3D"3689">5. PSR-7 : HTTP Message Interface=
</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3691" data-end=3D"4010">
<li data-start=3D"3691" data-end=3D"3763">
<p data-start=3D"3693" data-end=3D"3763">D=C3=A9finit des interfaces pour r=
epr=C3=A9senter les requ=C3=AAtes et r=C3=A9ponses HTTP.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3764" data-end=3D"3813">
<p data-start=3D"3766" data-end=3D"3813">Utilis=C3=A9 largement dans les fr=
ameworks modernes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3814" data-end=3D"3949">
<p data-start=3D"3816" data-end=3D"3949">Prise en charge des m=C3=A9thodes =
immuables (les objets HTTP ne changent pas, une nouvelle instance est retou=
rn=C3=A9e en cas de modification).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3950" data-end=3D"4010">
<p data-start=3D"3952" data-end=3D"4010">Permet d=E2=80=99=C3=A9crire des m=
iddlewares ind=C3=A9pendants du framework.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4012" data-end=3D"4015">
<h3 data-start=3D"4017" data-end=3D"4052">6. PSR-11 : Container Interface</=
h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4054" data-end=3D"4235">
<li data-start=3D"4054" data-end=3D"4141">
<p data-start=3D"4056" data-end=3D"4141">Interface standardis=C3=A9e pour l=
es conteneurs d=E2=80=99injection de d=C3=A9pendances (DI container).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4142" data-end=3D"4187">
<p data-start=3D"4144" data-end=3D"4187">Facilite l=E2=80=99interop=C3=A9ra=
bilit=C3=A9 des conteneurs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4188" data-end=3D"4235">
<p data-start=3D"4190" data-end=3D"4205">Deux m=C3=A9thodes :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4208" data-end=3D"4235">
<li data-start=3D"4208" data-end=3D"4220">
<p data-start=3D"4210" data-end=3D"4220"><code data-start=3D"4210" data-end=
=3D"4220">get($id)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4223" data-end=3D"4235">
<p data-start=3D"4225" data-end=3D"4235"><code data-start=3D"4225" data-end=
=3D"4235">has($id)</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4237" data-end=3D"4240">
<h3 data-start=3D"4242" data-end=3D"4285">7. PSR-12 : Extended Coding Style=
 Guide</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4287" data-end=3D"4548">
<li data-start=3D"4287" data-end=3D"4323">
<p data-start=3D"4289" data-end=3D"4323">Extension et mise =C3=A0 jour de P=
SR-2.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4324" data-end=3D"4372">
<p data-start=3D"4326" data-end=3D"4372">Recommandations plus d=C3=A9taill=
=C3=A9es pour le style.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4373" data-end=3D"4491">
<p data-start=3D"4375" data-end=3D"4491">G=C3=A8re aussi les espaces blancs=
, les d=C3=A9clarations <code data-start=3D"4423" data-end=3D"4428">use</co=
de>, les lignes vides, la visibilit=C3=A9 des propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9s/m=C3=A9t=
hodes, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4492" data-end=3D"4548">
<p data-start=3D"4494" data-end=3D"4548">C=E2=80=99est la norme actuelle re=
command=C3=A9e pour le style PHP.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4550" data-end=3D"4553">
