nd=3D"6278">PHP-CS-Fixer</strong> : corrige automatiquement le code selon l=
es r=C3=A8gles PSR.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6336" data-end=3D"6411">
<p data-start=3D"6338" data-end=3D"6411"><strong data-start=3D"6338" data-e=
nd=3D"6353">IDE/=C3=A9diteur</strong> : la plupart (PHPStorm, VSCode) ont d=
es int=C3=A9grations PSR.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6413" data-end=3D"6416">
<h3 data-start=3D"6418" data-end=3D"6440">2. Composer et PSR</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6442" data-end=3D"6545">
<li data-start=3D"6442" data-end=3D"6478">
<p data-start=3D"6444" data-end=3D"6478">Composer g=C3=A8re l=E2=80=99autol=
oading PSR-4.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6479" data-end=3D"6545">
<p data-start=3D"6481" data-end=3D"6545">Les packages Packagist respectent =
majoritairement ces standards.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6547" data-end=3D"6550">
<h3 data-start=3D"6552" data-end=3D"6575">3. Tests et qualit=C3=A9</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6577" data-end=3D"6715">
<li data-start=3D"6577" data-end=3D"6666">
<p data-start=3D"6579" data-end=3D"6666">Utiliser les outils CI (GitHub Act=
ions, GitLab CI) pour v=C3=A9rifier la conformit=C3=A9 aux PSR.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6667" data-end=3D"6715">
<p data-start=3D"6669" data-end=3D"6715">Int=C3=A9grer la validation PSR da=
ns les pipelines.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6717" data-end=3D"6720">
<h2 data-start=3D"6722" data-end=3D"6764">Partie 5 : Avanc=C3=A9 =E2=80=93 =
PSR et architecture</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"6766" data-end=3D"6769">
<h3 data-start=3D"6771" data-end=3D"6813">1. PSR dans les architectures mod=
ernes</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6815" data-end=3D"7082">
<li data-start=3D"6815" data-end=3D"6904">
<p data-start=3D"6817" data-end=3D"6904">Les PSR-7 et PSR-15 (middleware HT=
TP) permettent de cr=C3=A9er des middlewares ind=C3=A9pendants.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6905" data-end=3D"6997">
<p data-start=3D"6907" data-end=3D"6997">PSR-11 facilite l=E2=80=99utilisat=
ion d=E2=80=99injection de d=C3=A9pendances dans des architectures flexible=
s.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6998" data-end=3D"7082">
<p data-start=3D"7000" data-end=3D"7082">Le respect des PSR favorise la cr=
=C3=A9ation d=E2=80=99applications modulaires et maintenables.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7084" data-end=3D"7087">
<h3 data-start=3D"7089" data-end=3D"7142">2. Cr=C3=A9er vos propres interfa=
ces conformes aux PSR</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7144" data-end=3D"7271">
<li data-start=3D"7144" data-end=3D"7216">
<p data-start=3D"7146" data-end=3D"7216">Inspirez-vous des conventions PSR =
pour d=C3=A9finir vos propres interfaces.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7217" data-end=3D"7271">
<p data-start=3D"7219" data-end=3D"7271">Respectez les r=C3=A8gles de nomma=
ge et de documentation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7273" data-end=3D"7276">
<h3 data-start=3D"7278" data-end=3D"7305">3. Participer =C3=A0 PHP-FIG</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7307" data-end=3D"7390">
<li data-start=3D"7307" data-end=3D"7336">
<p data-start=3D"7309" data-end=3D"7336">Proposez des am=C3=A9liorations.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7337" data-end=3D"7390">
<p data-start=3D"7339" data-end=3D"7390">Adoptez les PSR d=C3=A8s leur sort=
ie pour rester =C3=A0 jour.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7392" data-end=3D"7395">
<h2 data-start=3D"7397" data-end=3D"7410">Conclusion</h2>
<p data-start=3D"7412" data-end=3D"7735">Les <strong data-start=3D"7416" da=
ta-end=3D"7423">PSR</strong> sont indispensables pour tout d=C3=A9veloppeur=
 PHP souhaitant produire du code professionnel, maintenable, et interop=C3=
=A9rable. Ma=C3=AEtriser ces standards vous permettra de collaborer efficac=
ement, d=E2=80=99int=C3=A9grer des biblioth=C3=A8ques tierces sans heurts, =
et d=E2=80=99=C3=A9crire un code conforme aux meilleures pratiques de l=E2=
=80=99=C3=A9cosyst=C3=A8me PHP.</p>
<p data-start=3D"7737" data-end=3D"7886">N=E2=80=99h=C3=A9sitez pas =C3=A0 =
utiliser les outils de validation PSR dans vos projets et =C3=A0 toujours r=
especter ces recommandations, m=C3=AAme pour des projets personnels.</p>
