<hr data-start=3D"2097" data-end=3D"2100">
<h3 data-start=3D"2102" data-end=3D"2150">4. Bonnes pratiques pour les test=
s unitaires</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2152" data-end=3D"2474">
<li data-start=3D"2152" data-end=3D"2202">
<p data-start=3D"2154" data-end=3D"2202">Tester un seul comportement par m=
=C3=A9thode de test.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2203" data-end=3D"2294">
<p data-start=3D"2205" data-end=3D"2294">Utiliser des assertions claires (<=
code data-start=3D"2238" data-end=3D"2252">assertEquals</code>, <code data-=
start=3D"2254" data-end=3D"2266">assertTrue</code>, <code data-start=3D"226=
8" data-end=3D"2286">assertInstanceOf</code>, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2295" data-end=3D"2371">
<p data-start=3D"2297" data-end=3D"2371">Nommer les m=C3=A9thodes de tests =
de mani=C3=A8re descriptive (<code data-start=3D"2350" data-end=3D"2369">te=
stAddReturnsSum</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2372" data-end=3D"2427">
<p data-start=3D"2374" data-end=3D"2427">Garder les tests rapides (pas de d=
=C3=A9pendances lentes).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2428" data-end=3D"2474">
<p data-start=3D"2430" data-end=3D"2474">Isoler les d=C3=A9pendances avec d=
es mocks/fakes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2476" data-end=3D"2479">
<h3 data-start=3D"2481" data-end=3D"2536">5. Gestion des d=C3=A9pendances d=
ans les tests unitaires</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2538" data-end=3D"2743">
<li data-start=3D"2538" data-end=3D"2604">
<p data-start=3D"2540" data-end=3D"2604">Utiliser <strong data-start=3D"254=
9" data-end=3D"2565">mock objects</strong> pour simuler des d=C3=A9pendance=
s externes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2605" data-end=3D"2701">
<p data-start=3D"2607" data-end=3D"2701">=C3=89viter l=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s a=
ux bases de donn=C3=A9es ou services externes directement dans les tests un=
itaires.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2702" data-end=3D"2743">
<p data-start=3D"2704" data-end=3D"2743">Exemple d=E2=80=99un mock simple a=
vec PHPUnit :</p>
</li>
</ul>
