<hr data-start=3D"5879" data-end=3D"5882">
<h2 data-start=3D"5884" data-end=3D"5937">Partie 4 : Techniques avanc=C3=A9=
es et bonnes pratiques</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"5939" data-end=3D"5942">
<h3 data-start=3D"5944" data-end=3D"5991">1. Int=C3=A9grer tests unitaires =
et fonctionnels</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5993" data-end=3D"6141">
<li data-start=3D"5993" data-end=3D"6043">
<p data-start=3D"5995" data-end=3D"6043">=C3=89quilibre entre tests rapides=
 et tests complets.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6044" data-end=3D"6085">
<p data-start=3D"6046" data-end=3D"6085">Tests unitaires pour la logique m=
=C3=A9tier.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6086" data-end=3D"6141">
<p data-start=3D"6088" data-end=3D"6141">Tests fonctionnels pour valider le=
s cas utilisateurs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6143" data-end=3D"6146">
<h3 data-start=3D"6148" data-end=3D"6180">2. Automatisation avec CI/CD</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6182" data-end=3D"6355">
<li data-start=3D"6182" data-end=3D"6269">
<p data-start=3D"6184" data-end=3D"6269">Int=C3=A9grer l=E2=80=99ex=C3=A9cu=
tion des tests dans un pipeline (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Jenkins).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6270" data-end=3D"6309">
<p data-start=3D"6272" data-end=3D"6309">Bloquer les merges si tests =C3=A9=
chouent.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6310" data-end=3D"6355">
<p data-start=3D"6312" data-end=3D"6355">G=C3=A9n=C3=A9rer des rapports de =
couverture de code.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6357" data-end=3D"6360">
<h3 data-start=3D"6362" data-end=3D"6387">3. Couverture de code</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6389" data-end=3D"6539">
<li data-start=3D"6389" data-end=3D"6461">
<p data-start=3D"6391" data-end=3D"6461">Utiliser <code data-start=3D"6400"=
 data-end=3D"6417">--coverage-html</code> avec PHPUnit pour visualiser la c=
ouverture.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6462" data-end=3D"6539">
<p data-start=3D"6464" data-end=3D"6539">Ne pas viser 100% =C3=A0 tout prix=
, mais =C3=A9viter les zones critiques non test=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6541" data-end=3D"6544">
<h3 data-start=3D"6546" data-end=3D"6586">4. Mocking avanc=C3=A9 et doubles=
 de test</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6588" data-end=3D"6742">
<li data-start=3D"6588" data-end=3D"6653">
<p data-start=3D"6590" data-end=3D"6653">Utiliser des mocks, stubs, spies, =
fakes pour isoler les unit=C3=A9s.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6654" data-end=3D"6742">
<p data-start=3D"6656" data-end=3D"6742">Composer avec les appels externes =
dans les tests fonctionnels via fixtures et sandbox.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6744" data-end=3D"6747">
<h3 data-start=3D"6749" data-end=3D"6791">5. Tests bas=C3=A9s sur des sc=C3=
=A9narios (BDD)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6793" data-end=3D"6936">
<li data-start=3D"6793" data-end=3D"6877">
<p data-start=3D"6795" data-end=3D"6877">Utiliser Behat ou PhpSpec pour =C3=
=A9crire des tests lisibles par les non-d=C3=A9veloppeurs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6878" data-end=3D"6936">
<p data-start=3D"6880" data-end=3D"6936">Favorise la collaboration entre d=
=C3=A9veloppeurs et m=C3=A9tiers.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6938" data-end=3D"6941">
<h3 data-start=3D"6943" data-end=3D"6972">6. Tests end-to-end (E2E)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6974" data-end=3D"7126">
<li data-start=3D"6974" data-end=3D"7044">
<p data-start=3D"6976" data-end=3D"7044">Testent toute la cha=C3=AEne, souv=
ent via navigateur (Selenium, Cypress).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7045" data-end=3D"7126">
<p data-start=3D"7047" data-end=3D"7126">Compl=C3=A8tent les tests fonction=
nels pour valider la vraie exp=C3=A9rience utilisateur.</p>
</li>
</ul>
